# Treinoway Web - Project Conventions

## UI Language

All user-facing text must be in **Brazilian Portuguese (pt-BR)**:

- Labels, buttons, placeholders
- Error messages and success messages
- Form validation messages
- User notifications

Code, comments, and technical documentation should be in English.

## No External Component Libraries

Do not use external component libraries. Use pure CSS with the existing design tokens defined in `src/index.css`:

```jsx
// ❌ WRONG
import { Button } from '@mui/material';
import { Card } from 'antd';

// ✅ CORRECT
<button className="btn-primary">Click me</button>
<div className="card">...</div>
```

## Authentication

Always use the `useAuth()` hook from `src/contexts/AuthContext.jsx`:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
import { useAuth } from '../contexts/AuthContext';

const Component = () => {
  const { user, isAuthenticated, hasRole, login, logout } = useAuth();
  
  if (hasRole('TRAINER')) {
    // Trainer-only logic
  }
};

// ❌ WRONG
const token = localStorage.getItem('accessToken');
const user = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('user'));
```

## HTTP Requests

Always use the centralized Axios instance from `src/api/axios.js`. Never use `fetch` or create new Axios instances:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
import api from '../api/axios';

const fetchData = async () => {
  const response = await api.get('/endpoint');
  return response.data;
};

// ❌ WRONG
import axios from 'axios';
const response = await axios.get('http://localhost:3000/endpoint');

// ❌ WRONG
const response = await fetch('http://localhost:3000/endpoint');
```

The centralized instance handles:
- JWT token attachment
- Token refresh on 401 errors
- Request/response interceptors

## Protected Routes

All authenticated routes must be wrapped with `<ProtectedRoute>` and `<Layout>`:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
<Route
  path="/profile"
  element={
    <ProtectedRoute>
      <Layout>
        <Profile />
      </Layout>
    </ProtectedRoute>
  }
/>

// ❌ WRONG
<Route path="/profile" element={<Profile />} />
```

## Console Statements

Do not leave `console.log` statements in final code. They are acceptable for temporary debugging only:

```jsx
// ❌ WRONG (in production code)
console.log('User data:', user);

// ✅ CORRECT (temporary debugging only)
// console.log('DEBUG: User roles:', user?.roles);

// ✅ CORRECT (for actual errors)
console.error('Failed to fetch data:', error);
```

## Error Handling Pattern

Always handle API errors with try/catch and display user-friendly messages in Portuguese:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
const [message, setMessage] = useState({ type: '', text: '' });

try {
  const response = await api.post('/endpoint', data);
  setMessage({ type: 'success', text: 'Operação realizada com sucesso!' });
} catch (error) {
  setMessage({ 
    type: 'error', 
    text: error.response?.data?.message || 'Erro ao realizar operação' 
  });
}
```
